# Environment files.
#
# .env, .env.development and .env.production are tracked deliberately: they hold
# only VITE_* values, which Vite inlines into the renderer bundle, so they are
# public by construction and the app cannot build without them.
#
# Everything else is ignored. This is the guard that matters: a service-role key
# or a Paddle/Resend secret dropped into .env.local is a full database bypass,
# and without this rule `git add -A` would commit it silently. Server-side
# secrets belong in Supabase edge-function secrets, never in this repo.
.env*
!.env
!.env.development
!.env.production

# electron-builder installer + unpacked output
release

